body:
Closing this in favour of #104 (the rebase of this branch onto main, which is parked behind #32).

@teknium1 parked this one - the approach as written kills healthy calls on models that answer with thinking `display: omitted` - and the rebase that followed was measured against real Claude Code 2.1.302 and found the same wall: a ping inside an open thinking block cannot tell thinking from stuck, because Claude Code emits its own pings about every 10 s and relays none of the upstream's. The signal that would work is the upstream's own progress, which needs the thinking stream to be visible (#32).

Nothing is lost by closing: the branch is still on salch-cred's fork (`fix-35-stall-watchdog`), and #104 carries the rebase. If this is picked up again it should start from the visible-thinking signal.
